      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "BERNINI 1.3B — one model, one complete schedule, one sampling call per chunk. Select wan2.1_bernini_1.3B_fp16.safetensors from Comfy-Org/Bernini-R. Do not load Wan base/Turbo weights or 14B LightX2V LoRAs. Load your source video and a saved clothing reference (e.g. Qwen Image Edit output). The reference feeds both the renderer and optional prompter. Prompt enhancer is disabled by default; enable only after selecting a vision model/server. Start max_seconds=5; change to 30 after checking quality. 16 fps, 81-frame chunks, 17 overlap. Loader video_info is connected so FPS stays synchronized. Saver frame_rate comes from Bernini. Sampling baseline: UniPC, simple, 40 steps, denoise 1, shift 3.0, conventional CFG 4.0. Single transformer/shift 3/UniPC follow the official 1.3B config; 40 steps follows the official CLI default. CFG 4 is a test starting point, not an equivalent to official multi-branch APG. Community 1.3B workflow reference: https://huggingface.co/neuregex/Bernini-1.3B-ComfyUI/blob/main/workflows/bernini_i2i_1.3B.json Official config: https://github.com/bytedance/Bernini/blob/main/configs/bernini_renderer_wan21_1p3b/config.json This native V2V adaptation does not require the community wrapper. GPU quality/speed is not yet benchmarked."
      ]
